From: ubuntu-rockchip build
Subject: [PATCH] config: enable PSI for Android containers (Waydroid/lmkd)

Waydroid itself only strictly needs binder/binderfs (already enabled),
but Android's lmkd relies on Pressure Stall Information (PSI) for memory
pressure handling since Android 10. Without CONFIG_PSI the container
still boots, yet low-memory killing degrades to legacy heuristics.

Enable PSI in the rockchip flavour config so kernels built from this
tree are fully ready for Waydroid/Anbox.

diff --git a/debian.rockchip/config/config.common.ubuntu b/debian.rockchip/config/config.common.ubuntu
--- a/debian.rockchip/config/config.common.ubuntu
+++ b/debian.rockchip/config/config.common.ubuntu
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@ CONFIG_TASKSTATS=y
 CONFIG_TASK_DELAY_ACCT=y
 CONFIG_TASK_XACCT=y
 CONFIG_TASK_IO_ACCOUNTING=y
-# CONFIG_PSI is not set
+CONFIG_PSI=y
 # end of CPU/Task time and stats accounting

 CONFIG_CPU_ISOLATION=y
